            formal: "💬 **Question**: Approach to debugging a production incident\n\n---\n\n⭐️ **Answer**: Well, honestly, when a production incident hits, I usually start by checking the monitoring dashboards and error tracking tools to see what's actually failing, you know? Then, I review recent deployments or config changes to see if something was just pushed. After that, I isolate the scope of the issue, check the logs, and roll out a quick fix or rollback if needed before doing a deeper root-cause analysis, right?"
