            formal: "💬 **Question**: Difference between HTML and CSS\n\n---\n\n⭐️ **Answer**: Well, basically, HTML is the structure of a webpage, right? It gives you all the elements like headings, paragraphs, and buttons. So, CSS is what you use to actually style all of that and make it look good, you know, handling things like layouts, colors, and responsive design."
